`load_data` takes a dataset configuration, a `TabularConfig`, `BIDSConfig` or `EmbeddingConfig` (or a `DatasetConfig` holding one), and no longer the same settings again as about 30 keyword arguments, nor `mode="auto"`. The two copies had drifted: `dtype` and `n_jobs`, settings of `BIDSConfig`, raised `TypeError: got multiple values for keyword argument` when passed as keywords. Only what a configuration cannot hold is still passed to `load_data`: `subject_metadata_df` and `subject_key` for BIDS data, `reader` and `id_fn` for embedding files. `load_data(config=...)` calls are unchanged.
